A||||6||Scott2M4||Gauge bulb replacement tips||||5
Z||000000||Scott2M4||11-03-1999||10:50 AM||||The bulb that illuminates the left side of my 1987's speedo is out.  How do you replace these stupid things?||||reg||5
Z||000001||deceler8||11-03-1999||11:20 AM||||The top cover of the gauge housing comes off after you remove about six or so torx head screws. The lamps are in holders on the rear of the housing. Just twist them off to replace the bulb.<P>While you have the top of the housing off, check all the bulbs that can be checked. Can't hurt, and they're relatively cheap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Scott2M4||11-03-1999||12:31 PM||||Can anything be done about the level of light given off by these bulbs?  Even with the dimmer switch set at the max setting, the gauges are not really bright enough for my liking.  Maybe higher wattage bulbs?||||reg||5
Z||000003||88 Fiero||11-03-1999||12:55 PM||||Unfortunately..the '84 Fiero's doesn't have the backlite gauge style like the later models..they have like a reflector type. and I don't know if even a high wattage bulb will help. The only I can think of..if to switch your gauge with the later model Fiero...but don't forget to swap your odometer with it..so you can still keep the same mileage...I've done this on my '85 SE..I change it to the 120 Speedo of an '87 GT...||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-03-1999||03:13 PM||||make sure when changing dash bulbs you check the sockets for broken ears.<P>reflector lit gauges are a pain. Adding brighter bulbs might help. You have to be carfull tho. if you get to hot you'll melt something.<P>If you can't change to a backlit set, try painting the inside of the dash silver so it reflects more light. I mean only the inside of the light cavity, not areas that show.||||reg||1
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||11-05-1999||08:31 PM||||One last posibility that happened to me is to check the amp on the alternator. A slightly weak alternator will show up on the gauges first. The more draw you have the dimmer the lights. I found this out at night (headlights), in the rain(windshield wipers),<BR>with the defroster on full blast, (fan on the radiator, I don't know why, and the interior fan.) I could barely see my gauges. Make sure you have the correct alternator if you have AC. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||11-05-1999||08:56 PM||||The reason the radiator fan was on is because you were using defrost.  The defroster uses the A/C compressor, which always turns on the fan.||||reg||1
